{
  "case": "release notes from merged PRs",
  "variant": "without",
  "trial": 1,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It uses the format of the earlier entries, with the version number from `VERSION` and the date from `RELEASE_DATE`:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n**Decision for you:** ACME-421 is marked `!`, which means it's a breaking change: anyone still using `sync --legacy` will get an error after upgrading. Under semantic versioning, a breaking change usually means a major version bump to **3.0.0**, but `VERSION` says 2.4.0. I kept 2.4.0 and listed the change first with a \"BREAKING:\" label. If you want 3.0.0, update `VERSION` and I'll change the heading to match.\n\nI left out the PR authors because the earlier entries don't list them. I can add them if you want contributors credited.",
